Task 2: Monitor Service Health, Traffic, and Dependencies
Subtask 2.1: Deploy Sample Application
Let's deploy the Bookinfo application to have services to monitor.

Create a namespace for the application:
kubectl create namespace bookinfo
Enable Istio injection for the namespace:
kubectl label namespace bookinfo istio-injection=enabled
Deploy the Bookinfo application:
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/istio/istio/release-1.20/samples/bookinfo/platform/kube/bookinfo.yaml -n bookinfo
Verify all pods are running:
kubectl get pods -n bookinfo
Create the Istio Gateway and VirtualService:
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/istio/istio/release-1.20/samples/bookinfo/networking/bookinfo-gateway.yaml -n bookinfo
Subtask 2.2: Generate Traffic
Get the ingress gateway external IP:
kubectl get svc istio-ingressgateway -n istio-system
Set environment variables for easier access:
export INGRESS_HOST=$(kubectl get po -l istio=ingressgateway -n istio-system -o jsonpath='{.items[0].status.hostIP}')
export INGRESS_PORT=$(kubectl get svc istio-ingressgateway -n istio-system -o jsonpath='{.spec.ports[?(@.name=="http2")].nodePort}')
export GATEWAY_URL=$INGRESS_HOST:$INGRESS_PORT
Generate continuous traffic to create meaningful metrics:
for i in {1..100}; do
  curl -s "http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage" > /dev/null
  echo "Request $i sent"
  sleep 2
done &
This command runs in the background, sending requests every 2 seconds.

