Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Kiali Dashboard Not Loading
Symptoms: Browser shows connection refused or timeout Solution:

# Check if port-forward is still running
ps aux | grep "kubectl port-forward"

# Restart port-forward if needed
kubectl port-forward svc/kiali 20001:20001 -n istio-system
Issue 2: No Traffic Showing in Graph
Symptoms: Empty graph or no edges between services Solutions:

Verify traffic generation is running:
# Check background processes
jobs

# Generate more traffic if needed
curl "http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage"
Check time range settings in Kiali (try "Last 1 minute")
Issue 3: Services Not Appearing
Symptoms: Expected services missing from graph Solution:

# Verify pods are running
kubectl get pods -n bookinfo

# Check Istio injection
kubectl get pods -n bookinfo -o jsonpath='{.items[*].spec.containers[*].name}' | grep istio-proxy
Issue 4: Metrics Not Updating
Symptoms: Stale or no metrics data Solution:

# Check Prometheus is running
kubectl get pods -n istio-system | grep prometheus

# Verify telemetry configuration
kubectl get telemetry -A
Advanced Configuration
Customizing Kiali Settings
Edit Kiali configuration:
kubectl edit configmap kiali -n istio-system
Common customizations:
Refresh intervals: Adjust data refresh rates
Graph settings: Default layout and display options
Tracing integration: Configure Jaeger settings
Setting Up Alerts
Create a custom dashboard configuration:
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: kiali-custom-dashboards
  namespace: istio-system
data:
  custom-dashboard.yaml: |
    title: Custom Service Health
    charts:
    - name: "Error Rate"
      spans: 6
      metricName: "request_total"
      dataType: "rate"
Cleanup
When you're finished with the lab, clean up the resources:

Stop traffic generation:
# Kill background curl processes
pkill -f "curl.*productpage"
Remove the circuit breaker rule:
kubectl delete destinationrule reviews-circuit-breaker -n bookinfo
Delete the Bookinfo application:
kubectl delete namespace bookinfo
Stop the port-forward:
# Press Ctrl+C in the terminal running port-forward
